<title>INDIA: India's RBI lowers repo auction cut-off to 2.9 pct.</title>
<headline>India's RBI lowers repo auction cut-off to 2.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) on Monday said it set a cut-off rate of 2.9 percent at its repo auction of government securities, down from 3.5 percent at the last auction  </p>
<p>The RBI said it received 59 bids for 92.80 billion rupees, of which it accepted nine bids for 41.30 billion rupees.</p>
<p>The weighted average cut-off rate was 2.8432 percent.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
